(c) whether Government has assessed the impact of rising toll charges and fuel costs on transport operators, farmers and inflation; and
(d) whether Government proposes to rationalise toll charges and introduce a transparent, time-bound toll policy with public disclosure of toll revenues and concession periods?

(a) whether Government has achieved the targets under the National Sickle Cell Elimination Mission (NSCEM), particularly in Maharashtra and other high-burden States, if so, the details of screening, diagnosis and treatment during the last three years State-wise;
(b) the details of support proposed for free screening camps through medical institutions and voluntary organisations and measures to strengthen coordination with district health authorities for timely detection and follow-up of patients; and
(c) the status of the nationwide digital platform for real-time registration and monitoring of sickle cell patients and if not operational, the reasons therefor and the timeline for its implementation?

(a) whether Government is aware of complaints of higher electricity bills after installation of smart prepaid meters compared to conventional meters;
(b) whether any independent technical audit has verified the accuracy and billing methodology of smart meters, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the State-wise number of consumer complaints on smart meter billing during the last three years and action taken thereon;
(d) whether Government proposes to provide consumers the option of independent meter testing and conventional meters in unresolved billing disputes; and
(e) the safeguards and grievance redressal mechanisms to prevent erroneous billing and protect consumer interests under the Smart Meter National Programme?

(a) whether Government has achieved the objectives of the PM SVANidhi Scheme; 
(b) if so, the details of loans sanctioned, disbursed, repayment rates and beneficiaries during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise, including Maharashtra;
(c) the number of street vendors who have availed the second and third loan tranches, State-wise, and the criteria adopted for assessing their creditworthiness;
(d) whether Government has assessed the Scheme's impact on vendors' income, digital payments and financial inclusion, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the measures taken to expand PM SVANidhi coverage in small towns, peri-urban areas and major markets, particularly in the State of Maharashtra?

(a) whether India's increasing dependence on imported strategic industrial goods poses a serious economic and national security risk;
(b) the sectors where import dependence exceeds 50 per cent and the annual import bill incurred thereon;
(c) whether any time-bound roadmap has been prepared to achieve self-reliance in these sectors, indicating annual targets and budgetary support; and
(d) the measurable outcomes achieved under 'Make in India' and PLI Schemes in terms of domestic value addition, employment generation and export growth?

(a) the total expenditure incurred on the development of India's first hydrogen-powered train, including rolling stock and hydrogen infrastructure;
(b) whether any comparative techno-economic study has been conducted between hydrogen, battery-electric and fully electrified trains in terms of cost, efficiency, emissions and long term viability, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the details of hydrogen train projects approved and proposed across the country, route-wise;
(d) the availability and cost of green hydrogen for such projects; and
(e) the timeline for expansion, indigenous manufacturing achieved, expected operational and environmental benefits of the project?

(a) whether Government has notified new rules under the Telecommunications Act, 2023 and reviewed their impact on consumers, telecom operators and citizens;
(b) the details of concerns received regarding possible misuse of surveillance provisions, protection of personal data and citizens’ right to privacy;
(c) the outcome of any independent assessment conducted on cybersecurity preparedness of telecom networks, prevention of digital frauds and protection of critical communication infrastructure;
(d) the impact of these rules on small telecom providers, competition and consumer interests in the telecom sector; and
(e) the measures taken to ensure transparency, accountability and protection of citizens’ rights while implementing the new telecom framework?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the existing spectrum auction model and evaluated its impact on telecom affordability, competition and public revenue;
(b) whether Government has examined a revenue-sharing mechanism wherein a fixed share of telecom operators’ consumer billing revenue is contributed to the exchequer instead of relying mainly on spectrum auctions;
(c) whether any assessment has been made regarding the impact of such a model on consumer tariffs, telecom investment and service quality; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure that spectrum, a public resource, benefits citizens through affordable connectivity and transparent revenue generation?

(a) the steps taken to address the acute distress faced by dairy farmers, particularly in Maharashtra, who are reportedly selling milk below production cost due to rising feed, labour and input expenses;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of falling procurement prices, export uncertainty and seasonal oversupply on farmers' livelihoods;
(c) the details of synthetic milk and adulteration cases detected during the last three years, State-wise, and action taken against the offenders;
(d) the impact of restrictions on loose milk sales on small vendors and consumers; and
(e) the measures proposed to ensure remunerative milk prices, curb adulteration and protect dairy farmers' livelihoods?

(a) whether Government is aware of misleading advertisements by certain EdTech platforms promising "100 percent placements", high-paying jobs and unauthorised institutional affiliations;
(b) whether complaints have been received regarding fake Universities, unaccredited foreign tie-ups, invalid degrees and deceptive refund or loan policies during the last three years, if so, the details thereof;
(c) the action taken against such entities under the relevant laws;
(d) whether Government proposes stricter regulation of EdTech advertisements, placement claims and online educational institutions; and
(e) the measures taken to protect students from fraudulent educational platforms and degree mills?

(a) whether Government has assessed if Maharashtra's allocation under the Scheme for Special Assistance to States for Capital Investment (SASCI) is proportionate to its contribution to India's GDP, manufacturing output and tax revenues;
(b) the details of funds allocated, sanctioned, released and utilised by Maharashtra since 2020-21, year-wise;
(c) whether any independent audit has evaluated if SASCI has created additional capital assets rather than substituting States' own capital expenditure; and
(d) whether Government proposes to revise the allocation formula and enhance Maharashtra's share to address its growing infrastructure deficit and regional imbalances?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the petition before the Bombay High Court seeking a CBI probe into the alleged extraction of natural gas from ONGC's Krishna-Godavari Basin, reportedly causing a loss of about US$1.55 billion;
(b) the findings of the A.P. Shah Committee, the DeGolyer & MacNaughton (D&M) audit and other investigations;
(c) whether the claim of migratory gas legally permits extraction from adjoining licensed blocks;
(d) the steps taken to protect public sector hydrocarbon assets and prevent unauthorised extraction; and
(e) whether Government proposes to recover losses and initiate legal action against those found responsible, if any?

(a) whether the outstanding debt of the Delhi Metro Rail Corporation (DMRC) has exceeded ?30,000 crore and if so, the lender-wise details, including liabilities to Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), as on date;
(b) whether Government has assessed DMRC's capacity to service its existing and Phase-IV debt from operational revenues;
(c) details of financial assistance, including equity, grants and subordinate loans, provided by the Centre and Government of NCT during the last five years; and
(d) whether the mounting debt burden has resulted in or is likely to result in, higher metro fares and the measures proposed to ensure DMRC's financial sustainability without burdening commuters?

(a) whether Government is aware that heavy rainfall and waterlogging in Mumbai repeatedly disrupt suburban and long-distance railway services, causing cancellation, delays and severe inconvenience to lakhs of commuters;
(b) the number of trains cancelled, diverted and delayed during the recent monsoon, along with the financial loss incurred;
(c) whether recurring flooding exposes serious deficiencies in railway drainage, track resilience and disaster preparedness despite substantial investments indicating the details of funds sanctioned and utilised during the last five years on various projects; and
(d) the corrective measures, timeline and funds earmarked to modernise vulnerable railway infrastructure and ensure uninterrupted services during future monsoons?

(a) whether Government has formulated a comprehensive diplomatic strategy to safeguard India's strategic, energy and economic interests amid the ongoing Iran–USA–Gulf conflict;
(b) whether India has undertaken any diplomatic initiatives to promote de-escalation while maintaining balanced relations with Iran, the Gulf countries, Israel and the United States;
(c) the details of consultations held with major regional and global partners on ensuring uninterrupted energy supplies and maritime security; and
(d) whether Government proposes to prepare a long-term National West Asia Strategy to address emerging geopolitical challenges and protect India's strategic autonomy?

(a) whether Government has taken cognisance of the recurring collapse, caving-in and structural failures of newly constructed bridges, flyovers and National Highway projects across the country, including the recent incidents on the Delhi–Mumbai Expressway and other major infrastructure projects;
(b) the findings of investigations into these failures, including responsibility fixed on contractors, consultants and officials and the details of penalties, blacklisting, recoveries and criminal action initiated; and
(c) whether Government proposes to mandate independent third-party structural audits before inauguration and establish a national accountability framework with strict quality standards to prevent recurrence of such failures?

(a) the post-wise and department-wise number of contractual employees engaged by the New Delhi Municipal Council (NDMC) and the total period of their contractual engagement;
(b) the department-wise remuneration of contractual employees and the corresponding pay scales of regular employees performing similar duties;
(c) the steps taken to ensure the principle of "equal pay for equal work" and to regularise eligible contractual employees; and
(d) whether there is any difference in the pay structure and service conditions of contractual doctors and other contractual employees in NDMC, and if so, the reasons therefor?
