(d) the steps proposed to strengthen safety advisories, emergency support and global advocacy against xenophobia targeting Indians?

(a) the details of steps taken to introduce industry and start-up-oriented courses in IITs, IIMs and other higher educational institutions to promote entrepreneurship and job creation;
(b) the manner in which practical training on industry setup, investment, marketing, exports and Government schemes such as Startup India and MSME is being incorporated;
(c) the existing provisions to facilitate participation of students and start-ups from these institutions in Central Government tenders, including infrastructure, IT and services; and
(d) the measures taken to support student entrepreneurs in establishing startups and generating employment in the country?

(a) whether Government is aware that despite strong demand in rural, tribal and backward districts of Maharashtra such as Gadchiroli and Nandurbar, no new Kendriya Vidyalayas have been sanctioned due to non-receipt of so-called “feasible proposals” and the reasons for such inaction;
(b) the status of the existing Kendriya Vidyalayas in Maharashtra, including enrolment capacity, infrastructure gaps, teacher vacancies and unmet demand for affordable CBSE education, district-wise; and
