(d) the steps taken so far by Government to address public opposition and ensure transparency in decision-making for the project?

(a) whether Government has reviewed concerns that India’s foreign policy is projecting conflicting signals under the rubric of strategic autonomy;
(b) how continued energy trade and military engagements with Russia are being reconciled with India’s commitment to a rules-based international order and partnerships with western nations;
(c) whether Government has assessed if such positioning has weakened trust among partners and reduced India’s influence in its immediate neighbourhood; and
(d) the concrete diplomatic, economic and strategic measures proposed to counter growing external influence in South Asia and ensure a proactive and coherent foreign policy roadmap?

(a) whether Government is aware that the combined tax revenue of the Union and the States in Financial Year 2024-25, when averaged across the population, amounts to approximately ?51,000 per citizen annually, along with the trend in per-capita tax collections over the last five years;
